## Submission

Repo state **is** the submission. A tag marks exactly what you're submitting, the way a project marks a release, so work you merge afterward doesn't change what's graded. By end of day **{{ CP7_DUE_DAY }}, {{ CP7_DUE }}**:

1. Merge everything to `main`, then tag it and push the tag:
   ```
   git switch main && git pull
   git tag -a cp7 -m "CP7: infrastructure package"
   git push origin cp7
   ```
2. In Canvas, paste the tag's URL (`https://github.com/YOUR-ORG/YOUR-REPO/tree/cp7`) and add a **photo of your Stranger's Read sheet**: legible, flat page, good light.

To change the submission before the deadline (or for a revision), move the tag to the new state and push it again: `git tag -fa cp7 -m "CP7: infrastructure package"`, then `git push -f origin cp7`, and resubmit. The package is re-tested by a stranger in the Week-11 repo audit and becomes the foundation of your launch package (CP11).

